WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:06.210
A magical Dragon Blade, humanoid villains
controlled by Namaari, and a much darker ending

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:10.860
for Sisu are just some of the fascinating
scenes and storylines Disney cut from Raya

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.180
and the Last Dragon.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:16.359
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing and explaining all

00:00:16.359 --> 00:00:19.320
the deleted scenes from Disney's Raya you
never got to see!

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.170
We will, of course, be talking spoilers, so
take care.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:27.470
Before the Druun became the faceless swirling
mists of purple that we see in the final film,

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:31.890
the villains were going to be very, very different
– much more humanoid monsters a bit like

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:32.890
armoured giants, in fact.

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:35.660
And there's a great deleted scene from the
home entertainment release with these alternate

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:39.070
versions of the Druun that would have appeared
at the beginning of the movie in a chapter

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:40.620
called "Tail of the Dragon".

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:45.649
"For years we've been on our own, broken,
losing hope, with no one to protect us from

00:00:45.649 --> 00:00:47.010
the Druun."

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:49.760
"I don't have it."

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:55.380
"No one, but me."

00:00:55.380 --> 00:01:00.020
In this story, Raya was a mysterious warrior
known as "Dragon Blade" and her sword had

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.360
a dragon pendant from her father Benja.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:03.360
"Oh!

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:04.530
Dragon Blade."

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:08.299
Because these villains had a specific form,
they could be fought in a more conventional

00:01:08.299 --> 00:01:12.170
manner than the more ethereal Druun we see
in the final movie.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:17.049
Ordinary weapons were still ineffective against
them though and only Raya's magical sword

00:01:17.049 --> 00:01:21.579
"Dragon Blade", which she created herself,
could defeat these sentient villains.

00:01:21.579 --> 00:01:26.289
Raya's weapon had the ability to pierce their
armour and then a clicking device caused them

00:01:26.289 --> 00:01:29.579
to melt while green goo exploded from their
bodies.

00:01:29.579 --> 00:01:31.030
"What are you doing here?"

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:32.030
"I'm helping you."

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:33.200
"No I don't need your help.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.200
Look out.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:37.909
You need one of these...
to do this."

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:45.399
As an extra twist, these Druun were originally
controlled by Namaari who in early versions

00:01:45.399 --> 00:01:49.989
of the movie was more of a traditional Disney
villain in the vein of Maleficent or Cruella

00:01:49.989 --> 00:01:50.989
de Vil.

00:01:50.989 --> 00:01:55.109
The deleted scene goes on to show how Raya
has to improvise against the Druun when she

00:01:55.109 --> 00:01:58.529
keeps on losing her sword
– and I especially like how she uses the

00:01:58.529 --> 00:02:02.689
bell against them!

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:08.300
The scene also introduces Tuk Tuk as Raya's
trusted and crucial side-kick who, in a change

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:12.720
from the final film, she didn't meet when
he was a baby, but who helps her out of her

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.439
sticky situation when she's cornered by the
Druun.

00:02:15.439 --> 00:02:19.409
Which is intentionally kind of amusing given
her earlier comment to the villager who wants

00:02:19.409 --> 00:02:23.719
to help her fight:
"I'm sorry, I have to do this alone.

00:02:23.719 --> 00:02:25.099
I don't need a side-kick."

00:02:25.099 --> 00:02:29.269
And that deleted line, of course, highlights
Raya's evolution over the course of the film

00:02:29.269 --> 00:02:33.450
from a lone fighter to someone willing to
work with others.

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:38.459
These humanoid Druun also appear in another
deleted scene where Raya rescues a group of

00:02:38.459 --> 00:02:42.319
Kumandrans fighting each other on a bridge
from a Druun who's about to attack them.

00:02:42.319 --> 00:02:44.159
"Move your wagon."

00:02:44.159 --> 00:02:53.190
"No you move your wagon, I was here first."

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:54.579
"Grandma.

00:02:54.579 --> 00:03:04.280
Grandma, hurry, come on we gotta go."

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:10.239
We can also see from this cut scene that these
early versions of the Druun turn objects to

00:03:10.239 --> 00:03:14.590
stone by grabbing hold of them, as we see
the monster try to do to Raya's sword;

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:19.180
of course, that’s something the Druun do
to humans in the final film.

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:22.510
"Not this sword."

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:28.109
As we can see, Raya's original sword was magical
and resistant to the Druun's powers but, like

00:03:28.109 --> 00:03:32.670
her sword in the final film, this sword also
had the ability to extend and attack from

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:34.359
afar with a grappling hook.

00:03:34.359 --> 00:03:39.129
Now, despite their human-like form, these
Druun were still very resilient with the ability

00:03:39.129 --> 00:03:42.860
to regenerate limbs even after Raya breaks
them off.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:46.560
Another interesting detail from this deleted
scene is that it looks like, rather than meeting

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:49.200
the Ongis in Talon as she does in the final
movie,

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:53.610
Raya would have met them at this point in
her journey, as we see the hilariously mischievous

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:57.090
monkeys stealing the fruit the two Kumandrans
are throwing at each other.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.420
"Move your wagon."

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:00.409
"Move your wagon."

00:04:00.409 --> 00:04:05.090
In the end, Disney decided to abandon the
human-like take on the Druun in favour of

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:08.700
making the villains more of an amorphous,
faceless evil.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:13.400
Their connection to Namaari was also dropped
in favour of making Raya's human antagonist

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:17.370
more nuanced and developing her relationship
with Raya instead.

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:21.829
I can also see that, as cool as a magical
sword would have been, dropping that idea

00:04:21.829 --> 00:04:26.310
fits better with the final movie's theme of
Raya having to cooperate with others and trust

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:28.970
in them in order to save the day.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:33.780
And a deleted flashback scene to Raya's childhood
shows how the original movie's main theme

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:37.060
was centred on the notion of how hope can
inspire community.

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:41.389
"This is the Heart of the Dragon, a rare and
very special flower.

00:04:41.389 --> 00:04:46.060
Like the dragon, it's connected to water.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:48.300
Watch.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:52.780
And look.

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:56.110
Each flower responds to the light of the other."

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:58.100
"One flower made all of those light up?"

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:01.220
"Yes, one light can light a thousand more.

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:03.190
That's what the dragons did.

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:06.060
They inspired light and hope in all the people
around them."

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:07.940
"I wish the whole world could see this."

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.880
"Maybe one day you'll show them."

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:13.670
Although this is a sweet scene,
I wonder whether the implication that Raya

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:18.060
would be inspired to fix the world by the
Heart of the Dragon could have felt too reminiscent

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:22.319
of Moana who used the Heart of Te Fiti to
restore peace to her world.

00:05:22.319 --> 00:05:26.710
The Heart of Te Fiti was the green gem the
ocean gave to Moana who then lifted the curse

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:31.139
threatening her island when she returned the
stone to the lava demon Te Ka.

00:05:31.139 --> 00:05:35.330
Given there were already a number of similarities
between the two movies such as shapeshifting

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:39.099
deuteragonists, the importance of water, and
a faceless threat to the land,

00:05:39.099 --> 00:05:43.830
the Heart of the Dragon concept could have
made the comparisons with Moana a few too

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:44.830
many.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:48.300
Some fans of the movie have pointed out the
romantic tension between Raya and Namaari

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:49.539
in several scenes.

00:05:49.539 --> 00:05:51.419
"Hey there, Princess Undercut."

00:05:51.419 --> 00:05:55.880
And Raya's voice actress Kelly Marie Tran
has said that's also how she interpreted it,

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:58.620
though she added that "wasn't the official
Disney line".

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:02.539
And there seems to be a little more of that
frisson in an alternate version of the scene

00:06:02.539 --> 00:06:05.129
when Raya meets the grown-up Namaari for the
first time.

00:06:05.129 --> 00:06:06.610
"Oh, what's dripping, dewdrop?

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:09.580
Oh, I see you've finally made some friends.

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:11.220
It's good that you're reaching out.

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:13.270
So what are you up to?

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:16.440
You stole an ancient map and scrolls from
the royal library."

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:17.440
"Correction.

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:19.370
I was just borrowing them, indefinitely."

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:24.039
In the final film, this encounter takes place
in the Tail Temple where Sisu and Raya find

00:06:24.039 --> 00:06:27.690
the second piece of the Dragon Gem;
whereas in the deleted scene, it appears to

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:32.400
take place in the shipwreck, with Sisu donning
a disguise rather than shapeshifting into

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:33.470
human form.

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:35.710
"Why are you making me wear this?"

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:37.680
"I'm doing this to protect you."

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:38.680
"From who?"

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:39.680
"From everyone.

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:43.260
We have to sneak into five different hostile
nations."

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:46.470
"In my day there were no nations.

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:48.590
Kumandra was one large, happy.."

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:49.590
"Namaari."

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:54.000
And in contrast to the more Indiana Jones-style
escape out of the cave we see in the final

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:58.910
film, in this alternate version Raya uses
a trick from Tuk Tuk to clear a path through

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:01.300
Namaari's soldiers.

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:02.490
"Dinnertime!"

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:03.690
"What?

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:06.009
It's like three o'clock in the afternoon,
why would you yell dinner.."

00:07:06.009 --> 00:07:09.370
"Come on!"

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:14.539
During the alternate chase scene, Raya and
Sisu also stop to recover a Dragon Gem piece

00:07:14.539 --> 00:07:15.810
at the bottom of a well.

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:17.240
"I sense a gem piece.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:18.240
There."

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:21.950
And Raya spills a catch of fish to distract
Namaari's big cats so that she can go and

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:23.770
collect the stone.

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:24.770
"Oh!

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:28.220
What the binturi are you doing?"

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:29.220
"There!

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:30.220
That well.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:31.220
Erm.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:32.220
Raya?"

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:33.220
"Catch!"

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:34.220
"Aha!

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.230
Shapechange power, it's back!"

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:40.770
Although this looks like a fun scene, it seems
to overcomplicate the getaway from Namaari

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:45.580
and also kind of crams in the shapeshifting
power reveal giving it less importance, so

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:47.780
I can see why it was cut.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:52.389
In the final movie, after Raya and Sisu escape
from Namaari, they end up on the Shrimporium,

00:07:52.389 --> 00:07:54.939
a boat restaurant run by Boun.

00:07:54.939 --> 00:07:57.219
"Welcome to the world-famous Shrimp-orium.

00:07:57.219 --> 00:07:58.219
My name is Boun.

00:07:58.219 --> 00:07:59.490
I'll be your server today.

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:01.719
Would you like to hear our daily specials?"

00:08:01.719 --> 00:08:02.719
"Yes, please!"

00:08:02.719 --> 00:08:07.500
However, in an earlier version of the movie,
Boun was "a Mr Fix-It who owned a scrapyard"

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:11.580
and Raya met him before she even met Sisu
when she was looking for someone to fix a

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:15.820
crack on Tuk Tuk's plate after a piece of
Druun arm got stuck inside.

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:18.520
"That mean I can get things fixed here?"

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:19.520
"Depends.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:20.520
What needs fixing?"

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:21.520
"It's my pill bear here.

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.520
He's got a crack."

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:23.520
"Who doesn't?"

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:24.580
"That came out wrong."

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:29.080
In this deleted version of the story, we also
discover that Boun is secretly hoping to team

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:32.159
up with the legendary Dragon Blade warrior
to defeat Namaari.

00:08:32.159 --> 00:08:33.460
"Nice target set up.

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:34.730
Not a lot of hits.

00:08:34.730 --> 00:08:35.760
Is that Namaari?"

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:36.760
"Hey!

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:37.760
Nothing to see here.

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:39.390
It's part of a secret mission I'm working
on.

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:43.910
If you have to know, I'm teaming up with Dragon
Blade to take down Namaari and the Druun.

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:44.910
"Dragon Blade?"

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:49.900
"Yeah, Dragon Blade, Defender of the Five
Lands, slays Druun with his deadly sword,

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:52.240
that has a dragon pendant swinging off of
it."

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:55.000
"Nope, can't say I've heard of him."

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:59.640
As often happens in animation, and as we've
seen with many Disney movies including Zootopia,

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:05.290
Frozen, and Moana, the studio often drastically
shifts and changes storylines even relatively

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:06.830
late in a movie's production.

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:12.000
And at one point, Raya's filmmakers seriously
considered a much darker, bittersweet ending

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:13.280
for the movie.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:17.400
Disney always planned to have Sisu die so
that Raya would come to understand that she

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:21.180
couldn't just rely on a magical dragon to
save Kumandra.

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:25.500
However, in an alternate ending, Sisu would
have remained dead, so she wouldn't have been

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:29.060
resurrected even after the rain fell and banished
the Druun.

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:35.230
In that ending, none of the dragons were resurrected,
making Sisu quite literally the Last Dragon.

00:09:35.230 --> 00:09:39.030
That might have been more striking because
it would have solidified the sacrifice the

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:43.710
dragons made for Kumandra and made the impact
of human discord more long-lasting.

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:47.790
But the filmmakers wanted to go with a happy
ending, so they resurrected Sisu together

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:52.270
with all the other dragons to create, in their
words, "a big Disney moment that [makes] your

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:53.270
heart sing."

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:57.440
And if you want to learn about more amazing
alternate endings and deleted scenes for animated

00:09:57.440 --> 00:10:01.570
movies such as the deleted Mecha Furby from
The Mitchells vs The Machines or how Elsa

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:05.320
nearly died in Frozen 2,
then tap here to check out my full playlist.

